## Key Concepts

### Image as Numerical Data

Computers do not interpret images as visual objects. Instead, images are represented as numerical pixel values stored in multidimensional arrays.

### Image Resizing

Images are resized to fixed dimensions to ensure consistency and improve computational efficiency during model training.

### NumPy Array Conversion

Images are converted into NumPy arrays, allowing mathematical operations and preprocessing techniques to be applied.

### Flattening

Multi-dimensional image data is transformed into a one-dimensional feature vector suitable for traditional machine learning algorithms.

### Dataset Creation

Multiple processed images are combined into structured datasets where each row represents an image and each column represents a pixel value.

